    "_note": [
        "# Attacker Lesson 7: Wireless Sniffing",
        "## Summary",
        "Everything on the lab network travels over Wi-Fi, and Wi-Fi is a shared medium: anyone in range can listen. In this lesson you join the lab network and capture its traffic passively, without sending a single packet of your own.",
        "## Objectives",
        "- Connect to the lab AP with the WiFi form.\n- Start a passive capture with the Sniff form.\n- Use the IP source and destination columns to tell conversations apart.\n- Explain what an eavesdropper can learn without ever being detected.",
        "## Reading",
        "*Securing Cyber-Physical Systems: A Hands-On Guide*, Chapter 4: Wireless Networks, Commas, and \"Quotes\"",
        "## Where This Fits",
        "**Previous:** Attacker Lesson 2, *Network Recon*."
